                                    <div class="faq-section" style="margin-top:40px;">
                                        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                                        <h3>What is Assembly's biggest advantage?</h3>
                                        <p>Design-first product + adjacent-lifestyle content + aspirational-but-accessible positioning. Multi-dimensional advantage over pure product or pure marketing brands.</p>
                                        <h3>Assembly vs Mokobara — key differences?</h3>
                                        <p>Both accessible-premium travel. Mokobara more retail-scaled + broader category. Assembly more design-focused + community-driven. Coexist by strategy differentiation.</p>
                                        <h3>Can new travel brands compete?</h3>
                                        <p>Yes in specific niching (adventure-specific, women's travel, business-travel-specialty, luxury vegan). Category has room for multiple positioning.</p>
                                        <h3>Should aspirational D2C invest in retail?</h3>
                                        <p>Selective retail experiences (pop-ups + limited flagships) build brand equity. Full retail scale is different strategic choice.</p>
